# WN22-AU-000050: Windows Server 2022 permissions for the System event log must prevent access by nonprivileged accounts.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-au-000050-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 permissions for the System event log must prevent access by nonprivileged accounts.`
    description `Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The System event log may be susceptible to tampering if proper permissions are not applied. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,file-acl,ntfs,ksi-mla-osm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-OSM,NIST-800-53:AU-9`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-OSM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the permissions on the System event log file (System.evtx) to prevent access by nonprivileged accounts. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement: Eventlog - Full Control SYSTEM - Full Control Administrators - Full Control The default location is the "%SystemRoot%\System32\winevt\Logs" folder. If the location of the logs has been changed, when adding Eventlog to the permissions, it must be entered as "NT Service\Eventlog".`

    component_id `comp-windows-file-acl`

    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-OSM by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Windows\System32\winevt\Logs\System.evtx does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AU_9 `Windows Server implements AU-9 by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Windows\System32\winevt\Logs\System.evtx does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        path `C:\Windows\System32\winevt\Logs\System.evtx`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE exists_check
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_1
        allow_identities string not_contains `Users`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_2
        allow_identities string not_contains `Everyone`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_3
        allow_identities string not_contains `Anonymous`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_4
        allow_identities string not_contains `Guest`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_5
        allow_identities string not_contains `INTERACTIVE`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF exists_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_3
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_4
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_5
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
